0. PREAMBLE
========================================================================

The software, source code, object code, binaries, configuration files,
containers, container images, documentation, diagrams, UML models,
screenshots, illustrations, reports, technical writings, presentations,
data models, database schemas, playbooks, scripts, and any other work
of authorship contained in, distributed with, or associated with the
ARGUS project (collectively, the "Software") are the exclusive
intellectual property of the Author, TBINI Mustapha Amin (the "Author").

The Software was produced as part of a summer internship performed by
the Author during the second year of the engineering cycle at TEK-UP
University, within the premises of Gérance Informatique (the "Host
Company"). The Software is delivered as an academic deliverable and is
NOT open-source, NOT free software, and NOT public domain.

By accessing, viewing, downloading, cloning, forking, reading, copying,
compiling, executing, referencing, citing, or otherwise interacting
with any portion of the Software, YOU (an individual, a group of
individuals, an entity, a company, an organization, an educational
institution, a government body, or any automated system, artificial
intelligence, machine-learning model, agent, crawler, scraper, or
robot acting on their behalf) explicitly and irrevocably agree to be
bound by every term of this License in its entirety.

If you do NOT agree to every term below, you are strictly forbidden
from accessing, downloading, cloning, forking, reading, copying,
compiling, executing, referencing, citing, or otherwise interacting
with any portion of the Software, and you must immediately destroy any
copy in your possession.

